---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAEcCwzuExy2fSCmH';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Product Operating Model Design | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Product operating model design for teams that have the strategy but not the system: portfolio to products to platforms to teams, with governance that enables and outcomes you can measure."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Leadership &amp; advisory</p>
      <h1>Turn strategy into a system that delivers.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For teams that know where they are going but are struggling to make
        it happen.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        You have bought the technology. You have a strategy deck. The board
        has seen the plan. But the organisation has not figured out the
        product and operational system around it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is the messy middle between strategy and execution. It is where
        most transformations stall. Not because of a lack of investment, but
        because nobody owns the whole chain from direction to outcome.
      </p>

      <h2>Sound familiar?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You have the strategy deck. Nobody can explain what it means for their team on Monday.</li>
        <li>AI capability acquired. No product thinking around it.</li>
        <li>Three reorgs in two years. The system still does not work.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I help you translate strategy into an executable system. Portfolio to
        products. Products to platforms. Platforms to teams. Teams to
        governance and measurable outcomes.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is especially effective around AI and data. Lots of
        organisations have acquired the capability without building the
        product thinking, team structure and decision-making system that
        turns technology into value.
      </p>

      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Strategy to portfolio translation</li>
        <li>Product and platform architecture aligned to business outcomes</li>
        <li>Team structure and operating model design</li>
        <li>Governance that enables, not bottlenecks</li>
        <li>Outcome frameworks you can actually measure</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Typically four to twelve weeks. Two or three days a week. Enough
        time to diagnose the system, design the operating model and
        establish the rhythms that keep it running after I step back.
      </p>
      <p>
        The engagement ends with an operating system your team can run
        independently, and governance rhythms that keep strategy connected
        to execution.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
        <p class="form-lede">
          If you have the strategy and the technology but the system around
          them is not working, that is the problem I solve.
        </p>
        <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="source" value="execution" />
          <div class="form-grid">
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Name</span>
              <input type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Email</span>
              <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </label>
          </div>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">What's this about?</span>
            <select name="topic">
              <option value="strategic-direction">
                Strategic direction
              </option>
              <option value="execution" selected>
                Execution &amp; transformation
              </option>
              <option value="fractional">Fractional leadership</option>
              <option value="advisory">Advisory</option>
              <option value="speaking">Speaking &amp; workshops</option>
              <option value="mentoring">Mentoring</option>
              <option value="other">Something else</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">Message</span>
            <textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
          </label>
          {
            TURNSTILE_SITEKEY && (
              <>
                <div
                  class="cf-turnstile"
                  data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY}
                  data-theme="light"
                />
                <script
                  is:inline
                  src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js"
                  async
                  defer
                />
              </>
            )
          }
          <button class="btn-plain" type="submit">Send it</button>
          <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
      <p class="faq-link">
        Questions first? <a href="/faq/">Read the FAQ.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <script>
    const ENDPOINT = 'https://contact-form.intentionaut.workers.dev/contact';
    const form = document.getElementById('contact-form');

    form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('form-status');

      try {
        const res = await fetch(ENDPOINT, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(data),
        });
        const result = await res.json();
        if (res.ok) {
          form.reset();
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.message || "Thank you; I'll reply soon.";
        } else {
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.error || 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
        }
      } catch {
        if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
